Interpersonal skills 
  Be prepared for Group Discussions
    Maintain:
      Clarity - Express your ideas clearly so everyone can understand them.
      Body Language - Maintain good posture, eye contact, and appropriate gestures.
      Listening - Listen carefully to others without interrupting them.
      Tone of voice - Speak confidently, calmly, and politely.
      Appropriate Language - Use respectful, professional, and easy-to-understand words.
      Courtesy - Respect everyone's opinions and allow others to speak.
      Conciseness - Express your points briefly without unnecessary details.
      Correctness - Share accurate information using proper grammar and facts
      Quality is more important than quantity
